verses.tf_en:
① **«وَلَقَدْ فَتَنَّا الَّذِیْنَ مِنْ قَبْلِهِمْ»** (And We certainly tested those who came before them;) — All preceding prophetic communities—from the followers of Nuh, Ibrahim, Musa, and 'Isa—endured fierce persecutions, boycotts, and martyrdoms for the sake of divine truth;
② **«فَلَیَعْلَمَنَّ اللّٰهُ الَّذِیْنَ صَدَقُوْا»** (so Allah will surely make known those who are truthful in faith,) — In His eternal knowledge, Allah already knows all things before they happen; here, "making known" means manifesting their steadfast sincerity in the realm of physical action so it becomes visible proof before all creation;
③ **«وَلَیَعْلَمَنَّ الْكٰذِبِیْنَ»** (and He will surely expose the hypocritical liars.) — Demonstrating those whose faith collapsed at the first sign of worldly trial.

① **«مَنْ كَانَ یَرْجُوْا لِقَاۤءَ اللّٰهِ»** (Whoever yearns for the meeting with Allah...) — Whoever lives with deep longing to behold the divine countenance, receive His sacred pleasure, and inherit the everlasting reward of Paradise;
② **«فَاِنَّ اَجَلَ اللّٰهِ لَاٰتٍ»** (...then indeed the appointed time of Allah is surely arriving!) — Let him endure earthly trials with joyful patience, for the span of this mortal life is brief and the promised Day of Resurrection and reunion draws nearer with every breath;
③ **«وَهُوَ السَّمِیْعُ الْعَلِیْمُ»** (and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing.) — Hearing the prayers, sighs, and invocations of His lovers, and knowing the deepest devotions and sacrifices hidden in their hearts.

① **«وَالَّذِیْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ»** (And those who believe and work righteous deeds...) — Those who fortify their faith with pious conduct, regular prayer, charity, and ethical integrity;
② **«لَنُكَفِّرَنَّ عَنْهُمْ سَیِّاٰتِهِمْ»** (...We will certainly expiate from them their sins and misdeeds,) — Wiping away their past transgressions, faults, and minor slips through the washing of sincere repentance and good deeds;
③ **«وَلَنَجْزِیَنَّهُمْ اَحْسَنَ الَّذِیْ كَانُوْا یَعْمَلُوْنَ»** (and We will surely reward them according to the best of what they used to do!) — Multiplying their rewards and evaluating them on the standard of their highest, most sincere deeds.

① **«وَوَصَّیْنَا الْاِنْسَانَ بِوَالِدَیْهِ حُسْنًا»** (And We have enjoined upon man excellent kindness towards his parents;) — Filial devotion and honoring parents is one of the highest moral imperatives in Islam;
② **«وَاِنْ جَاهَدٰكَ لِتُشْرِكَ بِیْ مَا لَیْسَ لَكَ بِهٖ عِلْمٌ فَلَا تُطِعْهُمَا»** (“...but if they exert pressure upon you to ascribe partner with Me that of which you have no knowledge, then do not obey them!”) — This verse was revealed regarding Sayyiduna Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him): when he accepted Islam, his mother Hamnah went on a hunger strike, vowing to starve to death unless he apostatized. Allah laid down the eternal Islamic legal canon: *La ta'ata li-makhluqin fi ma'siyatil-Khaliq* ("There is no obedience to any creature in disobedience to the Creator"). One must remain respectful and gentle, yet completely firm against committing idolatry or sin;
③ **«اِلَیَّ مَرْجِعُكُمْ فَاُنَبِّئُكُمْ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ»** (Unto Me is your ultimate return, and I will inform you of all that you used to do.) — On Judgment Day, every parent and child will stand accountable before Allah for their faith and conduct.

① **«وَمِنَ النَّاسِ مَنْ یَّقُوْلُ اٰمَنَّا بِاللّٰهِ»** (And among mankind are some who say: “We believe in Allah;”) — Describing weak-willed opportunists and hypocrites who claim Islam in times of ease;
② **«فَاِذَاۤ اُوْذِیَ فِی اللّٰهِ جَعَلَ فِتْنَةَ النَّاسِ كَعَذَابِ اللّٰهِ»** (but when they are persecuted in the cause of Allah, they equate the torment of men with the punishment of Allah!) — Fleeing from worldly hardship as if it were the eternal fire, compromising their religion to escape transient ridicule or pain;
③ **«وَلَئِنْ جَاۤءَ نَصْرٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّكَ لَیَقُوْلُنَّ اِنَّا كُنَّا مَعَكُمْ»** (Yet if victory and triumph come from your Lord, they certainly protest: “Indeed, we were always with you!”) — Eagerly demanding their share of war spoils and communal prestige;
④ **«اَوَلَیْسَ اللّٰهُ بِاَعْلَمَ بِمَا فِیْ صُدُوْرِ الْعٰلَمِیْنَ»** (Is not Allah fully cognizant of all that resides in the breasts of the entire creation?) — Divine omniscience easily pierces their facade, knowing the hypocrisy festering beneath their outward claims.

① **«وَقَالَ الَّذِیْنَ كَفَرُوْا لِلَّذِیْنَ اٰمَنُوا اتَّبِعُوْا سَبِیْلَنَا»** (And the disbelievers said to those who believed: “Follow our path...”) — The pagan aristocrats urged the early Muslims to abandon Islam and revert to the ancestral polytheism of the Quraysh;
② **«وَلْنَحْمِلْ خَطٰیٰكُمْ»** (“...and we will carry your sins for you!”) — Promising that if resurrection and judgment were real, they would assume all liability and punishment on their behalf;
③ **«وَمَا هُمْ بِحٰمِلِیْنَ مِنْ خَطٰیٰهُمْ مِّنْ شَیْءٍ»** (Yet they cannot carry the slightest fraction of their sins;) — A hollow, impossible guarantee: in the divine court, no soul can bear the burden of another;
④ **«اِنَّهُمْ لَكٰذِبُوْنَ»** (indeed, they are sheer liars!) — Uttering deceptive promises that will be shattered on the Day of Judgment.

① **«وَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا نُوْحًا اِلٰی قَوْمِهٖ»** (And We certainly sent Nuh to his people...) — Illustrating prophetic perseverance for the early oppressed Muslims through the story of the first Messenger of firm resolve;
② **«فَلَبِثَ فِیْهِمْ اَلْفَ سَنَةٍ اِلَّا خَمْسِیْنَ عَامًا»** (...so he remained among them for a thousand years minus fifty years;) — Sayyiduna Nuh (peace be upon him) spent nine hundred and fifty years preaching day and night with immense patience, facing generation after generation of mockery, stoning, and insult;
③ **«فَاَخَذَهُمُ الطُّوْفَانُ وَهُمْ ظٰلِمُوْنَ»** (then the Deluge seized them while they were persistently wrongdoing.) — When their defiance became absolute, the catastrophic Great Flood engulfed their world, wiping the haughty oppressors from the face of the earth.

① **«اِنَّمَا تَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ اَوْثَانًا وَّتَخْلُقُوْنَ اِفْكًا»** (“You merely worship idols besides Allah, and you invent sheer falsehoods;) — Exposing the absurdity of paganism: carving stones with their own hands and then inventing myths of divine power around them;
② **«اِنَّ الَّذِیْنَ تَعْبُدُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ لَا یَمْلِكُوْنَ لَكُمْ رِزْقًا»** (“Indeed, those you worship besides Allah possess no power to give you any sustenance;”) — The carved statues cannot provide a single grain of wheat, a drop of rain, or a breath of life;
③ **«فَابْتَغُوْا عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ الرِّزْقَ وَاعْبُدُوْهُ وَاشْكُرُوْا لَهٗ»** (“...so seek your sustenance exclusively from Allah, worship Him alone, and be grateful to Him;”) — Direct your hopes, supplications, and devotions to the sole Provider (*ar-Razzaq*);
④ **«اِلَیْهِ تُرْجَعُوْنَ»** (“...unto Him you shall all be returned!”) — For eternal accounting.

① **«قُلْ سِیْرُوْا فِی الْاَرْضِ فَانْظُرُوْا كَیْفَ بَدَاَ الْخَلْقَ»** (Proclaim: “Travel through the earth and observe how He originated creation;) — Encouraging scientific contemplation and geological/historical observation of the cosmos to witness the wonders of divine genesis;
② **«ثُمَّ اللَّهُ یُنشِئُ النَّشْأَةَ الْآخِرَةَ»** (“...then Allah shall bring forth the final creation in the Hereafter;”) — Just as He initiated the primeval cosmic creation, He shall resurrect all humanity for the everlasting life of the Hereafter;
③ **«اِنَّ اللّٰهَ عَلٰی كُلِّ شَیْءٍ قَدِیْرٌ»** (“...surely Allah possesses supreme power over all things!”) — His omnipotence encompasses every possibility, and nothing in existence can resist His sovereign command.
